# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv
env/
venv/

# Secrets / environment config (Marketplace API key, etc. — see plan.md)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test / type-check / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Vector / db stores only (Chroma/LanceDB, DuckDB/SQLite PUF backends).
# NOTE: the downloaded corpus under data/ is intentionally committed, not ignored.
*.duckdb
*.sqlite3
.chroma/
.lancedb/

# The LanceDB vector store (~41 MB: 6,722 chunks x 1,536 float32). Same reasoning as
# chunks.jsonl below — a pure function of committed inputs, rebuilt by `make embed` — with one
# addition: rebuilding it costs a paid embedding call, so the committed
# data/processed/vectors_meta.json records the embedding model, the dimensionality, the row count
# and the chunk snapshot ids it was built from. `make embed-check` verifies the store on disk
# still matches that manifest without re-embedding anything.
# This pattern is deliberately spelled out rather than relying on `.lancedb/` above: that one is
# dot-prefixed and does NOT match this path.
data/lancedb/

# Raw Medicare publication PDFs (~44 MB of binaries) — the one exception to the rule
# above. data/raw/medicare_pubs/catalog.json records the url, sha256, and Last-Modified
# of every file, so `uv run python scripts/download_medicare_pubs.py` reproduces this
# directory exactly. The manifest and the processed text corpus ARE committed.
data/raw/medicare_pubs/pdf/

# Exchange PUF zips/CSVs (~410 MB for plan year 2026 alone — Benefits & Cost Sharing is a
# 375 MB CSV) and the derived Parquet mirror. data/raw/exchange_puf/catalog.json records
# each file's url, ETag, Last-Modified, sha256, and row/column counts, so
# `uv run python scripts/download_exchange_puf.py` reproduces both directories exactly.
# The manifest and the small per-state sample under processed/exchange_puf/sample/ ARE
# committed.
data/raw/exchange_puf/*/*.zip
data/raw/exchange_puf/*/*.csv
data/processed/exchange_puf/*/*.parquet

# Part D SPUF extracts (~86 MB of pipe-delimited text per quarter, 58 MB of it the basic-drugs
# formulary file's 1.12M rows) and the derived Parquet mirror. data/raw/part_d_spuf/catalog.json
# records each member's url, byte offset and length inside the 2.49 GB container, CRC32, sha256,
# and row/column counts, so `uv run python scripts/download_part_d_spuf.py` reproduces both
# directories exactly. The manifest and the small contract-anchored sample under
# processed/part_d_spuf/sample/ ARE committed.
data/raw/part_d_spuf/*/*.txt
data/processed/part_d_spuf/*/*.parquet

# The chunked corpus (~7 MB). Unlike every exception above, this one is not about size — it is
# that chunks are a pure offline function of the committed corpus.jsonl files, rebuilt in about a
# second by `make chunk`, and they churn end-to-end on every parameter tweak.
# data/processed/<source>/chunks_meta.json IS committed and records the input sha256, the
# parameters, and the output sha256, so the ignored file is exactly reproducible and any drift is
# a test failure (tests/test_chunks.py::test_chunks_match_committed_manifest).
# Committing the chunks would also double-count every advisory licensing hit in `make scan` —
# chunk text is a verbatim subset of corpus text, so the counts would become a number about
# chunking parameters rather than about the corpus.
data/processed/*/chunks.jsonl

# Eval run outputs. Generated artifacts, per frontend_plan.md §5.2 — a run is a measurement of a
# retriever at a moment, not a source of truth, and the runner rebuilds one on demand. Committing
# them would also put whatever an answerer produced under the public-repo guardrail's review.
data/eval_runs/

# Frontend build tooling. This block MUST exist before the first `npm install`, and that ordering
# is load-bearing rather than tidy: scripts/scan_sensitive.py scans every tracked-or-untracked-
# and-not-ignored file for credential and PII markers repo-wide (only the licensing markers are
# scoped to data/). npm dependency trees routinely ship *.pem and *credentials* test fixtures,
# which fire the BLOCKING cred:secret-filename marker on filename alone, and thousands of author
# e-mail addresses, against a pii:email baseline of 0. Ignoring first puts all of it out of scope
# by construction — the same mechanism that keeps .env and the raw PDFs out.
# frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts is generated but IS committed, so the repo type-checks without
# running the backend (frontend_plan.md §3).
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
